      "keysecondary": [],
      "comment": "Hale's marks",
      "content": "Two snakes in knotwork meet at Hale's throat. They mark the oath he swore on Aldric's blade. A healed cut took out one snake's eye. The old arrow wound below his right collarbone is a separate scar. The cut across his left palm came from the oath and was left bare. The keel at his sternum records a company brought home, vouched for by Marten. Ansel vouched for the band around his left wrist after Hale's first winter alone. The line on his right forearm records his part in getting men through a wreck. Brannic vouched for the forge mark on the left. The back of the right hand has a watch lattice. Three short lines at the knuckles mark fair fights. The raven between his shoulders is for a dead man he carried off the ford. A loop at the left knee marks a fallen enemy whose eyes he closed. Under his clothes, high on his thighs, he keeps lines for the people he has lost. Soirsa's has an extra cut.",
